@startuml ClinicForecastingPlatformV2ServingSequence

title Clinic Forecasting Platform - Immutable v2 Serving Sequence

autonumber

actor Operator
participant "Role-specific batch CLI" as BatchCLI
participant "Role-specific batch pipeline" as Batch
participant "Local model registry" as Registry
participant "Serving snapshot" as Snapshot
database "Immutable serving store" as Store
actor Client
participant "FastAPI /v2" as API
participant "Serving provenance" as Provenance

== Produce a serving run ==

Operator -> BatchCLI: run_role_specific_batch.py
BatchCLI -> Batch: run_role_specific_batch(config)
Batch -> Batch: validate data + calibrate intervals
Batch -> Batch: forecast attended/completed/scheduled targets
Batch -> Batch: apply frozen hybrid target selection
Batch -> Batch: derive staffing + monitoring
Batch -> Store: write latest.csv convenience aliases
Batch -> Registry: register target-specific model versions
Registry --> Batch: versioned registry records
BatchCLI -> Snapshot: snapshot_role_specific_serving_run(...)
Snapshot -> Store: copy immutable forecasts/staffing/monitoring
Snapshot -> Store: fingerprint inputs/config/source/artifacts
Snapshot -> Registry: read exact model-version records
Snapshot -> Store: write immutable manifest.json
Snapshot -> Store: update latest_manifest.json
Snapshot --> BatchCLI: ServingRunManifest(run_id)
BatchCLI --> Operator: print serving run + manifest path

== Serve a v2 request ==

Client -> API: GET /v2/forecasts | staffing | monitoring | provenance
API -> Provenance: load latest_manifest.json
Provenance -> Store: read + validate manifest
Store --> Provenance: run_id + artifact fingerprints
Provenance --> API: validated ServingRunManifest
API -> Provenance: resolve_output_artifact(...)
Provenance -> Store: resolve path inside configured output root
Store --> Provenance: immutable artifact path
API -> Provenance: verify_file_fingerprint(path, expected)
Provenance -> Store: read size + SHA-256
Store --> Provenance: actual identity

alt path/size/hash mismatch
    Provenance --> API: error
    API --> Client: HTTP 503 fail closed
else artifact identity matches
    Provenance --> API: verified
    API -> Store: read immutable CSV artifact
    Store --> API: artifact rows
    API -> API: validate v2 schema + filter request window
    API --> Client: response + contract-version header + run-id header
end

note over API,Store
The API is read-only. It does not train models,
recompute the hybrid switch, or select a new model
inside request handling.
end note

@enduml
